---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import PolicyArticle from '../components/PolicyArticle.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import { policyLastUpdated, sitePayments } from '../data/policies';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms | She Who Remembers"
  description="Plain-language terms for using the She Who Remembers website, educational content, coaching pages, and related materials."
>
  <Hero
    heading="Terms"
    lede="Plain expectations for using this website and its educational content."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      These terms describe how this site is offered. They are website policy, not legal advice,
      and they are not presented as a lawyer-reviewed contract.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <PolicyArticle lastUpdated={policyLastUpdated}>
        <h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2>
        <p>
          By using this website, you agree to read these terms alongside the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/privacy')}>Privacy</TextLink> page, the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/coaching-disclaimer')}>Coaching Disclaimer</TextLink>, and
          the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/cancellation-refund-policy')}>
            Cancellation & Refund Policy
          </TextLink>
          . If you do not want to use the site on that basis, you can leave.
        </p>

        <h2>Educational purpose</h2>
        <p>
          This website offers coaching, educational material, reflection, and personal-development
          work connected to She Who Remembers. It is here to help you locate a threshold, understand
          the work, and choose a next step. It is not a clinic, a court, or an emergency service.
        </p>

        <h2>Coaching and courses</h2>
        <p>
          Course pages, private guidance, and related materials describe educational and coaching
          containers. Dates, fees, and enrollment details appear only when an offering is actually
          open. Browsing a description is not enrollment.
        </p>
        <p>
          A fit conversation is a conversation about fit. It is not pressure to buy, and it is not
          a guarantee that a container will be offered or that it will be right for you.
        </p>

        <h2>No professional-client relationship from browsing</h2>
        <p>
          Reading this website does not create a coaching, counseling, medical, legal, or other
          professional-client relationship. That kind of working relationship, if it happens,
          begins only through a clearly offered container and your agreement to take part in it.
        </p>

        <h2>No guarantees</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site promises a particular result: not healed relationships, not trauma
          resolution, not mental-health treatment, not spiritual awakening, not financial outcomes,
          and not guaranteed transformation. Insight is not the same as a changed life. You remain
          the one living the life.
        </p>

        <h2>Personal responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the choices you make after reading this material or taking part
          in the work. Support can clarify. It cannot take over authorship of your decisions.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Unless otherwise noted, original website copy, course materials, original exercises,
          educational materials, book content presented here, and branding on this site belong to
          She Who Remembers or to the people who hold those rights. You may read the public pages
          for your own use. You may not copy, republish, or sell those materials as if they were
          yours.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party materials remain with their owners. Messages you send through the contact
          form are not claimed as original She Who Remembers creative work simply because you sent
          them. They may be read in order to understand and, where appropriate, reply.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Use this site in a way that does not harm the work, other visitors, or the people who hold it. Do not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>attempt to break, overload, or misuse the site or its forms</li>
          <li>submit confidential medical, psychiatric, legal, or crisis material through the general contact form</li>
          <li>impersonate another person</li>
          <li>use the content to harass, defame, or exploit anyone</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>External services and links</h2>
        <p>
          This site may link to an external booking calendar, a form provider, or other pages this
          project does not operate. Those services have their own terms. She Who Remembers is not
          responsible for their content or their availability.
        </p>

        <h2>Purchases and paid offerings</h2>
        {
          sitePayments.publicCheckoutActive ? (
            <p>
              Paid offerings, when purchased through this site or a linked checkout, are subject
              to the terms shown before payment and to the Cancellation & Refund Policy.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              No public payment checkout is currently active on this site. When a paid offering
              is configured, the price, what is included, and the terms that apply will be shown
              before purchase. Until then, course and guidance pages do not complete a sale.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2>Cancellation and refund policy</h2>
        <p>
          Specific cancellation and refund terms depend on the offering. They will be shown before
          purchase or booking when a paid container exists. The current framework lives on the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/cancellation-refund-policy')}>
            Cancellation & Refund Policy
          </TextLink>{' '}
          page. This site does not invent windows, deposits, or &quot;all sales final&quot;
          language before those facts are known.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Pages, offerings, and scheduling availability can change. A description on this site is
          not a promise that a particular course, date, or private container will remain open.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation language</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent the law allows, She Who Remembers is not responsible for decisions you
          make after using this website or taking part in coaching or educational work. Nothing
          here is a promise of a particular result.
        </p>
        <p>
          This language is meant to be proportionate to a coaching, education, book, and course
          website. It does not ask you to waive rights that the law does not allow you to waive.
          It does not set a governing-law or arbitration rule, because those facts are not
          established on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Updates to terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated as the site changes. The date at the top of the article is
          the last time this wording was intentionally revised.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent through the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</TextLink> page.
        </p>
      </PolicyArticle>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If the question is the work itself"
    primary={{ label: 'Coaching Disclaimer', href: withBase('/coaching-disclaimer') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Contact', href: withBase('/contact') }}
  >
    <p>Terms describe use of the site. The disclaimer describes the limits of the work.</p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>
